# The `so101-tower` rig as a task family — the SO-101 follower with a wrist
# camera, bolted to the overhead camera tower, on a white desk.
#
# THIS IS THE SIM HALF OF THE PROJECT'S SIM-TO-REAL TRACK. The rig it models
# is the one `projects/so101-tower/` records with (`docs/camera-rig.md`,
# `docs/tutorials/so101_tower.md`): the base asset carries the wrist camera on
# the printed mount, the `tower` slot carries the overhead camera on its
# stand, and the props are the task's PRINTED bowl and brick
# (`tools/soarm/gen_tower_props.py`: one set of numbers for the print files
# and the sim assets; the recorded Duplo is `props/duplo_brick.xml`) on the
# desk. The two `<camera>`s are what the batched tracer renders for a
# pixel policy; nothing in the tabletop family has one.
#
# ⚠ THE SLOT TABLE IS THE BUDGET — see `so101_tabletop.family`. TWO free slots
# here, not three: nv = 6 + 12 = 18, which is also two fewer than what killed
# the family on Metal (nv 24, `sac_task_gpu.mojo`'s header).
schema_version=1
family=so101_tower
base=noeira/envs/robots/assets/so_arm101_tower.xml
horizon=300
# ⚠ 30, NOT 20: the rig records and deploys at 30 Hz (`meta/info.json`
# `fps`). `So101TowerConfig.FRAME_SKIP` restates it as 16 substeps of 2 ms
# (31.25 Hz — the nearest integer skip); a policy stepped here has the same
# cadence its real deployment will.
control_freq=30
# ⚠ THE BASE ASSET'S <option> IS RESTATED IN THE COMPOSED SCENE — MuJoCo
# ignores an attached child's option. `cone="elliptic" impratio="10"`: the
# sim grasp creeps out of the jaw under the defaults (see the bake).
inherit_option=1

# ⚠ A FILL LIGHT, SO THE WHITE PARTS STAY WHITE SEEN EDGE-ON. Under MuJoCo's
# default headlight (.1 ambient) the jaws render nearly black from the wrist
# camera: both lights graze them. The real room lights them from everywhere
# and the recorded wrist frames show them light grey-white. Chosen against
# the rig's undistorted real frames (2026-09-22): ambient .45 brings the jaws
# to a light grey without washing out the overhead view's shading (.6 did);
# the headlight's diffuse drops .4 -> .3 to keep the lit faces from clipping
# harder than they already do. Randomized around by `randomize.mojo`.
#
# ⚠⚠ SUPERSEDED 2026-09-24 BY AN APPEARANCE CALIBRATION against the printed
# recording (cube-in-bowl-printed, both cameras, surfaces labelled by MuJoCo
# segmentation at the recorded arm states). With the .7 sun and the headlight
# above, the desk rendered CLIPPED WHITE (255) on both cameras against the
# real 183 overhead / 155 wrist, the white arm parts 255 against 143, and
# `--dr full`'s darkest wrist frames never reached the real brightness (for
# series-2 H s1, blanking the real wrist image improved its roll 52.8 -> 39.5
# deg; a later student recovered the roll without this, so it is a fidelity
# fix, not THE roll fix). Fitted in MuJoCo, whose light model the tracer
# matches: ambient .6 from everywhere, NO headlight diffuse, a .2 sun — the
# room is lit diffusely — with the desk / arm / prop albedos lowered to the
# real grey levels (`desk_mat.xml`, bake step 6, `gen_tower_props.py`).
# Measured on the TRACER's frames after (real in brackets): frame mean
# overhead 130 (127), wrist 164 (146); desk 170 (183 / 155); arm 147 (143);
# bowl hue 38 (35); brick hue 217 / 203 (204 / 203). `--look legacy`
# (`so101_tower_rig.apply_tower_look`) renders the pre-calibration look,
# byte for byte, for an A/B.
headlight=0.6,0.0,0.5
sunlight=0.2

# ⚠⚠ THE ROBOT SITS ON THE STAND'S BASE PLATE, 5 mm ABOVE THE DESK. The desk
# is the floor plane; the tower's foot and plate rest on it. See
# `props/so101_tower_stand.xml` for where the plate's hole pattern is.
base_pos=0.0,0.0,0.005

# ⚠⚠ EVERY EPISODE STARTS WHERE THE REAL ARM RESTS, NOT AT qpos0. MuJoCo's
# qpos0 is the arm straight up — a pose the real follower never starts from.
# Measured on the kept episodes of BOTH rig recordings (frame 0:
# cube-in-bowl, 50, 2026-09-15; cube-in-bowl-printed, 70, 2026-09-24), in
# model radians through the measured joint zero
# (`robot/so101/sim_map.tower_follower_zero_deg`; the roll centre moved +5 deg
# with that zero's roll on 2026-09-25, and the jaw's centre and half-span with
# the gripper's measured line the same day — the same real 0.5..41% span):
# lift, elbow and wrist_flex
# sit on their FOLDED hard stops (sd < 0.5 deg: the median, no jitter); pan,
# wrist roll and the jaw are wherever the operator left them, so each episode
# draws them uniformly over the observed span (real-arm degrees: pan
# -3.3..70.0, roll 49.8..84.5; jaw 0..41% open). The second recording started
# at pan 28..70, past the first's -3..46, which is why the span is the union.
# Lift -109.4 deg is past the stock -100 limit: the rig's model widens the
# JOINT (not the actuator) to -110
# (`bake_so_arm101_tower.py` step 7). The draw is `sampler.sample_base_qpos`
# on the host and `placement/table.reset_task_slots` on the device.
base_qpos=0.394770,-1.908661,1.544271,1.342561,1.258746,0.310346
base_qpos_jitter=0.639826,0.0,0.0,0.0,0.303035,0.459539

# ⚠ THE FIXTURE CARRIES ITS POSE (see the tabletop family). The stand is
# placed at the NEGATION of the arm's position on its plate — body (+0.019,
# +0.077) — so the robot stays at the world origin and every SO-101 constant
# (reach, park, obs) keeps its meaning. The plate CHAINS onto the foot's end
# (the rig's owner's correction, twice; see the stand's header): the post
# then stands 10..13 cm to the arm's RIGHT (-y), IN LINE with its base, where
# the real one is — the recorded overhead frames show the arm beside the
# tower's foot at the bottom-left of the image.
slot=tower:static:noeira/tasks/assets/props/so101_tower_stand.xml:-0.019,-0.077,0.0
# The desk: 65 x 65 cm, top face at z 0.002, spanning x -0.06..0.59 (the arm
# and the tower foot stand on its BACK EDGE); the body/site stays at x 0.32 so the
# regions below keep their frame — the slab is offset inside the asset.
slot=desk:static:noeira/tasks/assets/props/desk_mat.xml:0.32,0.0,0.001
slot=bowl:free:noeira/tasks/assets/props/bowl.xml
slot=brick:free:noeira/tasks/assets/props/brick.xml

# ⚠⚠ `slot_geom=` ON EVERY FREE SLOT, so the device placement table is
# GENERATED (`pixi run gen-placement-tables`) rather than hand-written — the
# tabletop family lacks these and restates its radius in `family_config`.
# bottom_z, top_z, h_radius — PRINTED by `tools/soarm/gen_tower_props.py`,
# which also writes both assets and both print files from one set of numbers.
slot_geom=bowl:0.0,0.045,0.060614
slot_geom=brick:-0.0125,0.0125,0.0176777

park=10.0,0.0,50.0

# ⚠ THE SITE NAME IS THE COMPOSED ONE: `desk_` + `surface`.
#
# REGION RECTS ARE IN THE MAT SITE'S FRAME, whose origin is at world
# (0.32, 0, 0.002). `desk_top` spans world x 0.18..0.38, y -0.16..0.16 — the
# band the SO-101 reaches at desk height with room for a 6 cm bowl to sit
# fully on the mat. The 0.03 half-band is the tabletop family's, measured
# there (`task_reachability.mojo`); re-measure here before trusting a reach
# rate.
region=desk_top:site:desk_surface:-0.14,-0.16,0.06,0.16:0.03

# ⚠⚠ TWO STRIPS FOR `init=`, 12 cm APART — see the tabletop family for why
# a goal may name only region 0 on the device. The bowl (h_radius 0.0606)
# goes on the arm's LEFT and the brick on its RIGHT, as the 50 recorded
# episodes have them (bowl centre-left, brick right of it, in the overhead
# frames). A bowl drawn from `desk_left` and a brick from `desk_right` start
# at LEAST 0.12 - 0.061 - 0.018 = 4.1 cm apart edge to edge, on every draw,
# so `Near(brick, bowl, 0.045)` is FALSE at reset for every draw.
region=desk_left:site:desk_surface:-0.14,0.06,0.06,0.16
region=desk_right:site:desk_surface:-0.14,-0.16,0.06,-0.06

# THE REAL LAYOUTS (24 Sep): the printed-props recording's start poses, from the
# overhead pose estimator over all 70 episodes (`tower_pose_real_check`,
# projects/so101-tower/poses/cube-in-bowl-printed_start_poses.csv), world mm:
# brick x 104..370, y -239..+207; bowl x 134..456, y -228..+189, on EITHER side
# of the brick. The strips above hold 20/70 bricks and 17/68 bowls. These two
# cover them; APPENDED so desk_top stays region 0. Two different unanchored
# regions are clash-tested (h_radius sum 0.079 > Near's 0.045: the goal is false
# at reset). |y| <= 0.24: the bowl's rim stays inside the real desk (+y 0.29).
# The bowl stops at x 0.38 (95% of the real ones): beyond ~0.40 m from the base
# the expert's place IK misses by 7-23 mm (measured on 150 draws to x 0.46,
# where only 2/68 real bowls are).
region=desk_brick:site:desk_surface:-0.22,-0.24,0.05,0.21
region=desk_bowl:site:desk_surface:-0.19,-0.23,0.06,0.19
